    "title": "The Block and Litowitz Center Explore \"Vigil\" Through Art [Video] - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By nublockmuseum ,\n1 days ago The Block Museum’s collection is a resource for looking closely, asking questions, and thinking with others. In a recorded talk presented with Northwestern’s Litowitz Center for Enlightened Disagreement, three artworks open new ways to consider Vigil, George Saunders’s novel and the 2026–27 Campus Reading Program selection. The works do not illustrate the book. They bring its questions about truth, responsibility, and compassion into sharper focus. Read full article",
